hygiene|practices-of-cleanliness|NOUN|Practices of cleanliness|Practices that keep people and their surroundings clean to help prevent illness.|vệ sinh; việc giữ vệ sinh|The kitchen supervisor explained the importance of hand hygiene before food preparation.|Người giám sát bếp giải thích tầm quan trọng của việc vệ sinh tay trước khi chuẩn bị thức ăn.|Uncountable; personal hygiene, food hygiene. Hygienic is the adjective.|-
magnet|object-with-magnetic-attraction|NOUN|Object with magnetic attraction|An object that produces a magnetic field and attracts certain materials, such as iron.|nam châm|A small magnet held the shopping list against the fridge door.|Một nam châm nhỏ giữ danh sách mua sắm trên cửa tủ lạnh.|Countable; a magnet, magnetic poles. Magnets do not attract every kind of metal.|-
o’clock|exact-hour-expression|ADVERB|Exact hour expression|Used after an hour number to state a time with no minutes past that hour.|giờ; đúng ... giờ|The rehearsal ends at nine o'clock in the evening.|Buổi tập kết thúc lúc chín giờ tối.|Use with whole hours: nine o'clock, not nine thirty o'clock. The apostrophe may be straight or typographic.|0
upwards|towards-a-higher-position|ADVERB|Towards a higher position|In the direction of a higher place or level.|lên trên; hướng lên|Warm air carried the paper lantern upwards.|Không khí nóng đưa chiếc đèn lồng giấy lên trên.|Upwards is common in British English; upward is common in American English. Both can be adverbs.|0
will|future-prediction|VERB|Future prediction|Used to state what someone expects to happen in the future.|sẽ|The next train will arrive at the smaller platform.|Chuyến tàu tiếp theo sẽ đến sân ga nhỏ hơn.|Modal auxiliary followed by the base verb; no third-person -s. Negative will not or won't.|0
will|present-decision-or-promise|VERB|Present decision or promise|Used to express a decision made now or a promise about a future action.|sẽ; quyết định hoặc hứa làm|I will return your camera before the weekend.|Tôi sẽ trả máy ảnh của bạn trước cuối tuần.|Modal auxiliary plus base verb; I'll is the contraction of I will. Distinguish a promise from a neutral prediction.|1
will|determination|NOUN|Determination|The mental strength to continue trying to do something despite difficulty.|ý chí|Her will to finish the race remained strong after the delay.|Ý chí hoàn thành cuộc đua của cô ấy vẫn mạnh mẽ sau sự chậm trễ.|Usually uncountable; the will to do something, strength of will.|2
will|document-about-inheritance|NOUN|Document about inheritance|A document that states how a person's property should be dealt with after their death.|di chúc|The character in the novel left his collection to the museum in his will.|Nhân vật trong tiểu thuyết để lại bộ sưu tập của mình cho bảo tàng trong di chúc.|Countable; make a will, leave something in a will. This lexical description does not establish a document's legal validity.|3
